cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use paperkiln or the Architecture Atlas methodology, please cite it as below."
title: "paperkiln: papers in, running models out — an educational, research-capable LLM training stack with a pre-registered findings registry"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Reich"
    given-names: "Jonathan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JohnnyTeutonic/paperkiln"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - transformers
  - autograd
  - reproducibility
  - pre-registration
  - ablation-methodology
  - architecture-search
  - sparse-attention
  - CUDA
abstract: >-
  paperkiln is a readable C++ LLM training stack (tape, ops, Llama family,
  quantisation, GGUF export) paired with an arXiv-to-architecture extractor
  that attaches evidence snippets to every extracted value, and the
  Architecture Atlas: a findings registry in which every architecture claim
  is pre-registered before data exists, carries seed counts, paired tests
  and budget scopes, and where retractions and supersessions are published
  rows rather than deletions.
